Project Planning and Execution: Assist in developing and implementing project plans, schedules, and budgets.
Coordination and Communication: Coordinate activities with subcontractors, suppliers, and other stakeholders, ensuring effective communication and collaboration.
Document Management: Maintain accurate records and documentation, including RFIs (Requests for Information), submittals, and change orders.
Progress Monitoring: Track project progress, identify potential issues, and report on project status.
Cost Control: Assist in managing project costs and ensuring adherence to budget.
Quality Control: Assist in ensuring that projects meet required quality standards and specifications.
Safety Compliance: Ensure that all construction activities comply with relevant safety regulations and procedures.
Administrative Tasks: Perform administrative duties, such as preparing reports, setting up meetings, and managing correspondence. 
SKILLS:
Technical Skills: Understanding of construction methods, materials, and processes. 
Project Management Skills: Planning, organizing, scheduling, and managing projects effectively. 
Communication Skills: Strong written and verbal communication skills for interacting with various stakeholders. 
Problem-Solving Skills: Ability to identify and resolve issues that arise during the project lifecycle. 
Organizational Skills: Ability to manage multiple tasks and projects simultaneously, while maintaining accuracy and attention to detail. 
Software Proficiency: Proficiency in using project management software, such as Primavera P6 or Microsoft Project, and other relevant software. 
Analytical Skills: Ability to analyze data, identify trends, and make informed decisions. 
Leadership Skills: Ability to lead and motivate team members, while fostering a positive and collaborative work environment. 
Time Management Skills: Ability to prioritize tasks, meet deadlines, and manage time effectively. 
Client Relationship Skills: Ability to build and maintain strong relationships with clients and other stakeholders. 
